  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Infernal Stream sustain and burst (Lifesteal +10 ceiling, Damage +5 on two Lava rows)",
    "secondary": "Decrease Damage Taken on Lava Wave (+10 ceiling) and Afterburn pressure on Eruption Strike (+10 ceiling)",
    "tertiary": "Increase Damage Given (Lava Wave) and Increase Damage Taken (Blow of Devastation) as glue, +5 each",
    "rationale": "Suragu is a rank A Sustained DPS kit whose signature cast, Infernal Stream (60 AP, A rank), carries both of the tree's offensive anchors: Damage 40 and Lifesteal 40% on one action, so the burst and sustain routes both refine it while Magma Slayer (Damage 45) adds a second Damage row in PVP only. Lava Wave (40 AP ground circle) holds the kit's two self buffs, IDG 35% and DDT 30%, and anchors the tank route; Eruption Strike's Afterburn 35% (circle on the enemy, ally hazard) is the opt-in pressure route, and Blow of Devastation's IDT 35% is the cheap D-rank exposure that glues the offense Foundation together. Every percentage tag is a single row, so each takes Taiyo Kami's single-row maxima; Damage reaches two rows, one mode-restricted, so it stays at +5."
  },
